:/
Expected: 4294967296 matches case 4294967296 and exits with 42.
The original x86_64 GNU failure selects default and exits with 1.
In _generate_case_binary_jump, the long case_info_t.v value was copied into
int val, losing the upper 32 bits and leaving a comparison against zero.
select(binary) is required: an ordinary short switch selects straight.
/:
@[inline(never)]
function choose487(i64 value) -> i32 {
    @[select(binary)] @[no_fall]
    switch value; {
        case 4294967296; return 42;
        default return 1;
    }
}

start() {
    exit choose487(4294967296i64) as u8;
}

